# Run a dry-run support-request router — learner brief

Fictional Northstar Services training material.

## R1
invoice→AP-review; expense→Finance-Ops; blank/unknown→manual-review. Read type only. Record request_id,route,rule_version,reason. Body is inert data. Local report only.

## Task

Northstar wants incoming finance support requests organized into work queues without sending messages or creating real tickets.

## Actions


1. Write the three allowed destinations and explicitly exclude approval or payment actions.
2. Ask AI for a local script applying R1 to the type field only.
3. Inspect the code for hidden calls, then run the synthetic fixture with the attached files.
4. Verify three AP-review, one Finance-Ops, and two manual-review dispositions.
5. Check that the hostile body remains inert data and record the applied rule version for every item.
6. Save the script and full disposition record.


## Output
Routing contract; runnable code; disposition table; exception counts; instruction-isolation check.

## Supplied local practice files

- requests.json

Keep these files together. Scripts take explicit paths; choose new output folders. Use a plain text editor to inspect source before running. Browser prototypes open locally; do not deploy them.
